-- title:
--   Depth-zero Gauss order of varpiᵈux' in the crossing model
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a level $N\ge 1$, an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $q$, a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red}\colon A\to k$, modular polynomial data for $q$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence, the two Hecke integrality hypotheses $h\alpha,h\beta$, a place specialization $P$ for these data and a prolongation tuple $R$ over $P$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ and $w$ a place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\ k\ N$ over $k$, and assume the subring $B:=R.\mathrm{nodeIntegersOver}\ K\ w$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(Nq)$ (those functions lying in $R.\mathrm{nodeIntegers}\ w$ whose Laurent expansion lies in the $K$-rational field $\mathrm{NodeLocalized.fieldOver}\ (Nq)\ K$) is local. Let $\varpi$ be an element of the coefficient subring $A\cap K$, let $E\ge 1$, let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation domain with irreducible element $\pi$, and let $\iota$ be a ring isomorphism from the $\mathfrak{m}$-adic completion of $B$ onto the crossing model $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\ 2)\,W/\mathrm{uvCrossingIdeal}\ W\ (\pi^{E})$, carrying the constant $R.\mathrm{nodeConst}\ K\ w\ \varpi$ (the image of $\varpi$ under the structure map $A\cap K\to B$) to the class $\mathrm{const}\ (\pi^{E})\ \pi$ of the constant series $\pi$. Assume the order-reading law: for every $f\in B$ and $n\in\mathbb{N}$ with $R.\mathrm{nodeResidue}_2\ w\ f\ne 0$ of order $n$ at the place $\mathrm{arithFrobC}\ q\ k\ N\cdot w$, there is a unit $\gamma$ with $\iota(f)-\gamma\,U^{n}$ in the ideal generated by $\mathrm{const}\ (\pi^{E})\ \pi$ and $V$. Then for $x,x',u\in B$ with $R.\mathrm{nodeResidue}_2\ w\ u\ne 0$ of order $n$ at $\mathrm{arithFrobC}\ q\ k\ N\cdot w$, for $d\in\mathbb{N}$, and $x=(R.\mathrm{nodeConst}\ K\ w\ \varpi)^{d}\,u\,x'$, the Gauss orders taken with respect to $\mathrm{IsDiscreteValuationRing.addVal}\ W$, uniformiser $\pi^{E}$, weight $E$ and depth parameter $0$ satisfy $\mathrm{gaussOrder}(\iota x)=d+\mathrm{gaussOrder}(\iota x')$ in $\mathbb{N}\cup\{\infty\}$, where $\mathrm{gaussOrder}$ is the supremum of $\mathrm{repGaussOrder}$ over all lifts of the argument to $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\ 2)\,W$.
--
--   This is the end-valuation dictionary at one of the two branches of a node: at depth $0$ the Gauss-order function of the crossing model $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi^{E})$ adds the exponent $d$ of the constant $\varpi$ and is insensitive to factors whose second residue is nonzero. It is used in the construction of component charts and attached annuli for models of $X_0(Nq)$ and in the slope-drop computations that feed the component-group identities.
